            <div xml:id="d880">

                <pb facs="1070" n="960" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg960"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Nelson, Bert N./109: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-04T16:00:00+08:00">May 4, 1931—4 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 4—10:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>43. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 4, 3 p.m. My April 28, 1 p.m.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d880-f1"/> The
                            go-between returned to Hankow Saturday night and reported Ked brigands
                            declined to release Nelson and are insisting on delivery of 30 tins of
                            gasoline and in addition two sewing machines. Go-between returned to
                            Sungpu yesterday morning taking with him two sewing machines and 30 tins
                            of gasoline. He was accompanied to Sungpu by Nelson’s brother, Daniel
                            Nelson. Active military operations were started against the Ked brigands
                            in northeastern Hupeh several days ago by Government troops and several
                            towns including Chiliping, a communist stronghold, have been captured
                                <pb facs="1071" n="961" xml:id="pg961"/> by the troops under General
                            Li Ming-chung. It is hoped that Nelson may be released before these
                            operations reach the vicinity where he is now being held.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
